{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement","id":1375152,"title":"Princess the Hopeful Night Horror supplement","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-16T14:55:23-07:00","id":1375152,"title":"Princess the Hopeful Night Horror supplement","content":"Soooo a few years ago, I tried doing a supplement reflecting Hunters relationship with Princesses; The result was quite successful in getting people to participate, and resulted in Dark and Light, which you can find here:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1M2Y3OtDyWN3tVxE-pxAi4JCuuVAu3yMTt1khcL0ssNI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Now I would like to try starting a new project for a Princess supplement: namely a Night Horror style one, offering more rules and options for antagonists in Princess.<br /> <br /> Currently, I plan to title this one &quot;Tales from the Dark World&quot;, and as suggested by the title it would primarily focus on fleshing out the Darkness - though details for Twilight Princesses, Wardens, and Amanojaku, as well as new ideas for antagonists, are welcome as well.<br /> <br /> Ideally the supplement should at least provide:<br /> <br /> * New rules for the Darkness, including clear guidelines for creating Dark creatures, expanded Umbrae and Caligines, and possibly bonus powers for Dark Cults<br /> * Sample antagonists to use in your Chronicles, including Dark Creatures, Tainted areas and possibly others.<br /> <br /> If anyone is interested in taking part, let me know.<br /> <br /> Update: began working on the supplement. Here is the link, feel free to give feedback:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Dy3y2jh5xW7AppW89EKD683sik-49gWaQu-Q7iX8iQ8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Dy3y2jh5xW7AppW89EKD683sik-49gWaQu-Q7iX8iQ8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Dy3y2jh5xW7AppW89EKD683sik-49gWaQu-Q7iX8iQ8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Dy3y2jh5xW7AppW89EKD683sik-49gWaQu-Q7iX8iQ8/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 03-17-2020, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T16:24:37-07:00","id":1375166,"title":"","content":"an idea? More ideas For tainted places?<br /> <br /> Another option or two for attacking Tainted places<br /> <br /> I Miss the occult options that seem to have been excised<br /> <br /> List maybe a hundred ideas for tainted locations.<br /> <br /> <br /> but more ideas for Dark Creatures sounds good.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T17:16:54-07:00","id":1375179,"title":"","content":"Not a Princess player, but I might be tempted to try the line if this followed the trend of recent Night Horrors books and also included enough rules for certain antagonist-types of the line for them to be worthwhile player options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T19:49:21-07:00","id":1375211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1375166#post1375166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">an idea? More ideas For tainted places?<br /> <br /> Another option or two for attacking Tainted places<br /> <br /> I Miss the occult options that seem to have been excised<br /> <br /> List maybe a hundred ideas for tainted locations.<br /> <br /> <br /> but more ideas for Dark Creatures sounds good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I miss that option too^^<br /> <br /> And yeah, I do have a few ideas. I will need to write them down and flesh them out.<br /> <br /> @Inodiv: that can be arranged. I personally feel the Dark Template could use some stricter rules to build them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T19:57:09-07:00","id":1375213,"title":"","content":"Dethroned also should be looked at what they do with their time.<br /> <br /> And Servants of the Darkness in the Dreamlands...<br /> <br /> Oh How Sentient can a Actual Darkspawn , as opposed to Other kind of creature be? Some powers NEED Social interaction to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-16-2020, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T20:00:09-07:00","id":1375214,"title":"","content":"I keep on trying to get my own Night Horrors project off the ground for Princess. I actually did finally make the story background of a &quot;reverse Warden&quot;; a Dreamlander who was created by the Gales, became self-aware and that he was a prison guard for his &quot;daughter&quot;, absorbed the Warden who made him, and now leads a rampaging army of monsters he's conjured from the Gales to turn those caught by them into a nightmare they want to wake from. He's not a bad person, just caught in an endless existential crisis and not quite sure of the right thing. He does break people free from Galemarks, but he's an inexpert sort at best, and he's accidentally made one Dethroned because he didn't know when to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T04:38:42-07:00","id":1375256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1375213#post1375213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dethroned also should be looked at what they do with their time.<br /> <br /> And Servants of the Darkness in the Dreamlands...<br /> <br /> Oh How Sentient can a Actual Darkspawn , as opposed to Other kind of creature be? Some powers NEED Social interaction to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true. We'll need to adress this. Though I can at least already adress one: Darkspawns cannot be smarter than a trained guard dog.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I keep on trying to get my own Night Horrors project off the ground for Princess. I actually did finally make the story background of a &quot;reverse Warden&quot;; a Dreamlander who was created by the Gales, became self-aware and that he was a prison guard for his &quot;daughter&quot;, absorbed the Warden who made him, and now leads a rampaging army of monsters he's conjured from the Gales to turn those caught by them into a nightmare they want to wake from. He's not a bad person, just caught in an endless existential crisis and not quite sure of the right thing. He does break people free from Galemarks, but he's an inexpert sort at best, and he's accidentally made one Dethroned because he didn't know when to stop. </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to join here^^ maybe by combining our ideas we can both get somewhere;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 03-17-2020, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T06:42:31-07:00","id":1375275,"title":"","content":"How do I do breaks in a paragraph to answer part but only part of a question then another?<br /> <br /> If Darkspawn cant be smarter then a trained guard dog what happens when a darkened with a Caligae or umbrae relying on social interaction makes the transition to Darkspawn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T06:55:13-07:00","id":1375278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1375275#post1375275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I do breaks in a paragraph to answer part but only part of a question then another?<br /> <br /> If Darkspawn cant be smarter then a trained guard dog what happens when a darkened with a Caligae or umbrae relying on social interaction makes the transition to Darkspawn?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a &quot;quote&quot; section in the section to chose your police;<br /> <br /> as for the other question, these Caligines and Umbrae are meant for intelligent creatures of the Darkness like Cataphractoi or Mnemosyne, so my best guess is Darkspawns lose access to them when making the transition. A rule similar to Sanctify of Merits would probably apply.<br /> <br /> Anyway, started a doc for the supplement and began writing character creation rules for Darkened. I editted the first post so you can get the link directly here.<br /> <br /> Next I hope to work on creation rules for Antagonist Dark Creatures (you know, like most 2E books have). Just trying to figure out how I should do that, since Darks creatures don't have a Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 03-17-2020, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T08:06:16-07:00","id":1375281,"title":"","content":"another idea<br /> <br /> Not Directly to do with the Darkness but often enough happens in response to it?<br /> <br /> Maybe A System in the Dream lands to assemble an army?(Needing to be unique to the dreamlands only because Hopeful can act a good deal more openly there)<br /> <br /> Any hopeful spending signficiant time in the dreamlands is going to try hiring someone at some point.<br /> <br /> Oh theirs that one Cataphract with a Darkspawn Maid? Thought id mention that.<br /> <br /> It also said she was bestial when first recruited by him.<br /> <br /> And a breed of Darkspawn that were good people who did nothing. Shadow Puppets.<br /> <br /> Maybe some Darkspawn retain or regain a Degree of Sentience, like Pandorans can Become Sublimati.<br /> <br /> <br /> An idea on Wardens? Cover the Tiers From Rank 1 to Rank 5<br /> <br /> Idea for Rank 1 is a Warden who plays the role of a Fox or Stag perpetually on the run always 1 step away from the hunters.<br /> <br /> For Rank 5 Im thinking a Warlord That Keeps Drawing the hopeful into his narrative being distracted from their mission on earth in the process as they grow obsessed with stopping him.<br /> <br /> Oh how openly Should Wardens work with other Creatures of Darkness in the Dreamlands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-18-2020, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T05:24:09-07:00","id":1375414,"title":"","content":"Personally I think creature of Darkness in the Dreamlands should essentially work openly with each other, though Wardens would be the dominating ones (the Darkness in the Dreamlands are just a reflection after all).<br /> <br /> I am currently debating to decide if Darkspawns and others should be allowed to raise their Traits above 5. Again, no Supernatural trait, so that makes this hard to decide.Maybe Darkspawns and Mnemosyne couldn't, but Cataphractoi could? If so what defines their limit?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T09:52:17-07:00","id":1375449,"title":"","content":"I Think Cataphracts