-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1375808#post1375808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks^^ do you wish to write down the character's backstory yourself on the doc, or should I do this myself?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can. I'm in the middle of some stuff, I'll offer some suggestions once I see the full draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T08:19:55-07:00","id":1375813,"title":"","content":"Okay^^ thanks. Feel free to correct whatever I do later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T10:21:10-07:00","id":1375829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1375796#post1375796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> And interesting idea, though personally I'd make it a single character rather than a group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough at that works well I suppose.<br /> <br /> Id argue most or all Wardens should want such a ability though though only one needs to be actively looking for it.<br /> <br /> Oh another idea?<br /> <br /> Present a fully Developed Magister as a NPC Villain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-20-2020, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T08:23:48-07:00","id":1375972,"title":"","content":"Alright, we're starting to get somewhere. Started to work on the concepts suggested by Leliel.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> you think you can work on some slightly more elaborate summaries for your ideas?^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T11:35:06-07:00","id":1375989,"title":"","content":"Not sure on everything...<br /> <br /> Some Warden is looking for a way to procreate. many wardens may wish him the best, but their not interested in taking it out of their time To pursue such an etherial goal.<br /> <br /> The raise an army Thing... Im pretty sure would involve Presence+ Something+ Bonuses for how visible a threat is, or how accomplished you are.<br /> <br /> Was suggesting Write up a Magister as a NPC Villain an accomplished one with a lot of experience and 4 or 5 Princessses &quot;Retired&quot; By him.<br /> <br /> Oh!!!? An idea for a Fiction to go with it?<br /> <br /> Tale of a dethroning, and a nearly averted dethroning<br /> <br /> Always liked the idea of someone who regained a dot of belief, being tucked in gently as if they were still a small child.<br /> <br /> Before they go to sleep never to awaken and die in their sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 03-26-2020, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T04:56:27-07:00","id":1378503,"title":"","content":"Okay we did good progress, but the supplement could use some fleshing out. You guys feel free to follow the link and write your own suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T05:17:59-07:00","id":1378506,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of Princesses begin as members of the Twilight Courts, especially if they Blossom really young (like 13 or 14): Mirrors (if they\u2019re spoiled and a little self-centered), Tears (if they\u2019re depressed) or Storms (if someone hurt them and they\u2019re angry about it). Then as they mature a lot of them switch to the Radiant Courts: Hearts (romance and social interaction), Diamonds (intellectual stuff), Clubs (the earth and nature), Spades (jesters/tricksters) and Swords (passion).<br /> <br /> Not sure if this is exactly on topic, but maybe this will be helpful in your campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T08:11:32-07:00","id":1378547,"title":"","content":"Heres what I wrote up for a near miss on a Dethroned<br /> <br /> <i>They were Assembled as a Family for Their Comrade their Sister<br /> <br /> Their Elder Sister<br /> <br /> She\u2019d helped Unite them drawn them together protected them at great risk to herself<br /> <br /> But it had come at cost after cost to her Psyche to her Belief To her spirited<br /> She\u2019d Forgotten herself The light her Queen.<br /> <br /> They\u2019d Rallied on her desperate to keep her from a fate worse then death.<br /> <br /> They barely Succeeded<br /> <br /> She was now hugging her sister's one last time, not even remembering her own name<br /> but remembering that they were family<br /> <br /> One of them made sure the pillows were properly positioned with immaculate care<br /> <br /> finishing her hug not fully grasping at all how final this parting was she climbed into bed another tucked her in and turned off the light<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cGood night dear\u201d Was the last thing she heard before the final parting came.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-04-2020, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T10:18:25-07:00","id":1378575,"title":"","content":"Still think I perfer the way that Vocation does that. They don't die they come back to Belief 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T13:51:21-07:00","id":1378610,"title":"","content":"I Like how bittersweet it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T03:32:59-07:00","id":1378714,"title":"","content":"Longtime reader, first time poster.<br /> So I've been wondering what to post first &amp; I've decided to go with some darkspawn.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fleshcarvers&quot;: these were medical doctors that got corrupted by the Darkness. They have a visceral feel to them, thus explaining the possible name I came up with.<br /> <br /> Heirophants: religious leaders, will either be found at the head of a cult of the Darkness or other religious organization.<br /> Alternatively, one could be wandering the land, attaching itself to whatever religious group it finds, causing the group to gradually warp into something foul, then move on when there was nothing more to corrupt.<br /> <br /> The Whispering Dark: this, I envision, is a unique creature of the Darkness. It is spoken of only in rumors with no definite proof of its existence. The rumours that speak of it say that it recruits for something called the Court of Midnight.<br /> <br /> I will be posting stuff on the Court of Midnight, along with info on &quot;Saliga&quot; a country deep in the Dark World, tomorrow, my time, because it's pretty late where I am at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T06:49:52-07:00","id":1378745,"title":"","content":"hmmn a rather interesting idea...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:47:30-07:00","id":1378846,"title":"","content":"So. Saliga &amp; the Court of Midnight.<br /> For those of you who don't know, Saligia (turns out I got the spelling wrong, oh well) means &quot;salt&quot; in Latin. It is also an acronym for the Latin names of the seven deadly sins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:51:01-07:00","id":1378848,"title":"","content":"Saligia: A small country located somewhere deep in the Dark World, far from any doors to the material world. Its presence here, so deep in the Dark World is a source of many rumours &amp; the rare Noble who conclusively knows (not someone who has just heard the rumours) of its existence is troubled by the knowledge.<br /> This country has a very visceral feel to it (maybe, not so sure about this point now).<br /> The people struggle day in &amp; day out just to survive here.<br /> It is an oligarchy, ruled by a council comprised of the heads of the seven most powerful families. These seven families are each governed by one of the seven deadly sins (envy, gluttony, greed, lust, pride, sloth, wrath).<br /> The country also has these &quot;mini-provinces&quot; embodying other negative concepts/ideas/etc. like apathy, despair, violence, vanity, fraud, treachery, etc. It is possible for one of the &quot;mini-provinces&quot; to get a set at the table of the big seven, thereby knocking down one of the current houses, it would be very hard however. Food for thought.<br /> A while ago, it was found that the Inner Light of a Noble could be used to help Saligia survive, &amp; the country sent out teams of warriors, trackers, beasts, etc. to find some &amp; bring them back.<br /> Once a Noble has been delivered back to Saliga, a bloody sacrifice is performed, harvesting the Inner Light for the good of Saligia.<br /> Unbeknownst to Saligia, whilst performing bloody sacrifices of the Nobles provides large, strong bursts, should a Noble set down to live in Saligia their Inner Light would constantly leak into the country, albeit at a slightly weaker level. Oh they may have heard the theory, but why take the risk when they've already got a strategy that works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:52:03-07:00","id":1378849,"title":"","content":"The Court of Midnight: There are rumours of a Court of Nobles that cast their lot in with the Darkness, giving up &amp; electing to join the &quot;winning side&quot;. An impossibility to be sure, &amp; yet the rumours persist.<br /> <br /> Echo: people feel unsettled around this person, though they cannot pin why.<br /> <br /> Practical Magic: the Silver Tongue (persuasion) or the Iron Fist (intimidation). A Noble must choose one of these two upon joining the Court.<br /> <br /> Invocation: <br /> <br /> Orders: A series of dark parallels to the Protectorates &amp; Embassies, the Orders are each built to target a different Radiant or Twilight Court. There are rumours of other ones that target the Protectorates &amp; Embassies themselves, &amp; the other groups &amp; creatures in the CofD setting. Some possible Orders follow.<br /> <br /> The Order of Tarnished Images: targets the Nobles of Mirrors, building up their egos only to bring them crashing down. The members of the Order of Tarnished Images go out of their way to avoid recruiting because, just like their targets they have great egos &amp; can't stand the competition.<br /> <br /> The Order of Inverted Pentacles: oppose the Court of Pentacles.<br /> <br /> The Order of Eternal Childhood: targets Searchlight &amp; the Star of Bethlehem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:53:33-07:00","id":1378850,"title":"","content":"I was planning on doing all of that in one chunk, but ran into some difficulties, so three posts resulted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T14:57:12-07:00","id":1378851,"title":"","content":"Gonna have a think now about what my next post will be, but for anyone who would like to speculate about stuff, I'm leaning towards a pair of demon-blooded strains tied to Princess: The Hopeful. One born of the Light, &amp; the other born of the Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:01:15-07:00","id":1378853,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> I like your idea so far<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26055\" data-vbnamecard=\"26055\">Krat05</a> All these sound like really good ideas.I especially like the Whispering Dark and the Court of Midnight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:30:56-07:00","id":1378931,"title":"","content":"The Darkness Demon-Blooded<br /> The result of unusual &amp; unknown circumstances. What is known about the origin of this Strain, is that it was so circumstantial the odds of it being replicated are beyond microscopic.<br /> Despite the &quot;name&quot; (seriously, I do not consider &quot;the Darkness Demon-Blooded&quot; to be a proper name) the Darkness was not alone in the birthing this Strain. There were some people who got, let's say infected by the Darkness &amp; by the Light, almost simultaneously.<br /> The Darkness provided power &amp; the Light prevented the Darkness from making them just another group of darkspawn.<br /> Their Endowment is that they can use various Umbrae. One Umbrae per Endowment dot. However, their is a downside to this Endowment. The Darkness is still there, ever present, &amp; every time a Hunter of this demon-blooded strain uses an Endowment power, they must mentally fight against the Darkness with their Willpower. Failure does not mean that the power has failed, failure means that the Hunter's morality has taken a hit. Drop to one or possibly zero dots in morality, &amp; the Hunter is lost to become just another darkspawn, albeit one a bit more dangerous than the standard everyday darkspawn.<br /> Darkness Tainted places make fighting against this corruption harder, &amp; the morality will drop more than one dot.<br /> Because of this eternal, internal fight that they face, the Darkness Demon-Blooded have a reputation for being very understanding, forgiving, &amp; accepting, sometimes out doing even the Lucifuge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:31:43-07:00","id":1378932,"title":"","content":"The Light Demon-Blooded<br /> In all times there are people who experiment, pushing the boundaries of what is &amp; isn't possible.<br /> In the Kingdom, one such person tried infusing the Light in its most raw form into ordinary people. What the motivation was has been lost to time, what matters is that they succeeded, at the worst possible time, the fall of the Kingdom.<br /> In the Kingdom's absence, the various people who carried the Light in their bodies, they scattered to the winds.<br /> Over time they bred, had descendants, &amp; the Light was diluted, eventually only appearing in exceptional souls.<br /> At the same time the world grew harsher, less a place where the Light felt at home, so those inheritors learned how to fight, &amp; the Light was changed by this.<br /> These days when the Light appears, it is not the warm, comforting glow that the Queens remember or Nobles carry, it is the harsh, blinding spear of an angel.<br /> Look away for you will find no comfort here, for these are warriors with blood on their hands.<br /> There's a reason the combat-focused Calling of the Nobles is called &quot;Champion&quot; not &quot;Slayer.&quot; Well, these guys are the &quot;slayers.&quot;<br /> As a result of the Light in them, they have a measure of resistance against the corrupting influence of the Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:38:15-07:00","id":1378933,"title":"","content":"Extra info on the Light Demon-Blooded, regarding factions &amp; Endowment.<br /> <br /> Faction A: focuses on using archaic weapons.<br /> Faction B: focuses on using modern weapons.<br /> Faction C: focuses on strategy &amp; tactics.<br /> <br /> Hypothesized Possibilities for Endowment Powers<br /> Burn away illusions.<br /> Convince vampires they are standing in sunlight.<br /> See in the dark.<br /> Flashes of bright light.<br /> Very resistant to the Darkness, beyond the strain's norm (as long as your alive).<br /> A beam of light that can heal &amp; replenish a Noble, or damage a darkspawn.<br /> Combat-based Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:40:11-07:00","id":1378934,"title":"","content":"3 more antagonists tied to the Princess the Hopeful game.<br /> <br /> A low, persistent sound that is a remnant of the Kingdom from before it fell.<br /> It works its way into ordinary people, gradually getting them to be better than they were. You might think that this is a good thing with nothing bad about it, but the effects is basically brainwashing &amp; can cause many lives to be destroyed in the process.<br /> <br /> It was born when some &quot;Darkness fungi&quot; infected an apparently normal human being. The human, as it turned out, was Gifted &amp; the interaction between the fungus &amp; the supernatural capability they had (whatever it was) caused the person to turn into a humanoid fungal creature. Now they sit in their lair, which slowly grows, ruling over all they surview. Their power is at least equal to that of a Dethroned, as proven when they killed one that wandered into the lair.<br /> <br /> A former Mekhet which became trapped in the Dark World for a time. When they reemerged they were a thing made of shadows that drank positive &quot;feelings&quot; like hopes, dreams. It especially likes the taste of Inner Light, &amp; will target Nobles, Beacons, &amp; Sworn before others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T23:43:56-07:00","id":1378936,"title":"","content":"I'm currently all out of stuff that could fit on this thread. Moving over to an old thread titled Possible Host Concepts? for if anyone wants to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T16:26:21-07:00","id":1379090,"title":"","content":"These all are interesting ideas, but... aren't the first two more Hunters than Princess-specific antagonists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T16:57:20-07:00","id":1379098,"title":"","content":"Point. The Light-Blooded &amp; the Darkness-Blooded are more hunters than Princess-specific antagonists. They wound up on this thread because of how tied they are to Princess-specific elements &amp; because I can see Princess-specific antagonists originating from these strains extremely easily.<br /> Sorry if they don't seem at home on the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:32:59-07:00","id":1379104,"title":"","content":"Oh an idea? Some Crunch to the statement that by defeating Darkness in the Dreamlands you gain some insight Into darkness on earth?<br /> <br /> Rules letting you say... roll as per the omen sensitity merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-07-2020, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T19:55:08-07:00","id":1379384,"title":"","content":"Some more Princess: The Hopeful antagonists, these ones with a focus on the Darkness.<br /> <br /> A low-level spirit (but still high enough to be an individual spirit) of apathy that shows signs of something far darker. The spirit is consumed by the Darkness. Could turn up as the Totem of a werewolf pack (though that pack is going to have something off about it).<br /> <br /> An infectious, warped state of the Uratha. The condition originates in areas with sufficient levels of the Darkness &amp; is acquired by being bitten by one of them. How exactly the infection starts is mostly unknown, but true Uratha seem to be immune to catching it (at least by being bitten that is).<br /> Those afflicted come across as fairly normal most of the time (if rather asshole-ish). On the three nights of the full moon they turn into sadistic monster wolves that police the Gauntlet, acting completely without morality, decency, Harmomy, or anything.<br /> If the werewolf disease is removed the afflicted turns into a darkspawn.<br /> Oh &amp; they do remember what they do in wolf form &amp; do not lose control of themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T23:11:08-07:00","id":1379417,"title":"","content":"A couple of ideas for amanojaku that pose problems that regular amanojaku don't.<br /> <br /> This one came out of the Dreamlands through a different door than normal.<br /> They can enter other people's personal Astral space &amp; mess with stuff their, affecting morality, thought process, &amp; other stuff.<br /> <br /> And this one jumps into human bodies with disturbing ease, effectively not actually needing the possession magic other amanojaku use.<br /> It is a hedonistic sense freak, fully aware of how easily it can take over human bodies, &amp; takes no care of whatever body it has because it can always get a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T19:23:10-07:00","id":1379577,"title":"","content":"An idea on a Amojaku?<br /> <br /> One created deliberately by a Brat on a Defeated Magister after releasing the Nobles he'd 'retired' She retired him to the Dreamlands letting a dreamlander take his body<br /> <br /> That creates a lot of conflict I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:32:10-07:00","id":1379639,"title":"","content":"These are currently the last Princess-specific antagonists that I've come up with at the moment. These ones I consider not really, properly attached to Dreamlanders or the Darkness. That may change if they get properly developed.<br /> <br /> A weird affliction that effects Nobles, causing them to be driven to the unhealthy extreme of their Court's ideals/ideology/philosophy. The affliction does not have to result in Nobles going Dethroned, &amp; I think that it doesn't need to do that.<br /> <br /> A fallen Kingdom that does not realize its time has ended &amp; is trying to manifest itself in the physical world.<br /> <br /> A weapon created during the fall of the Kingdom. Designed with one purpose in mind: to fight the Darkness.<br /> The weapon was made by a Noble of Swords &amp; a Noble of Diamonds. It is immune to the taint of the Darkness, but that might be the only good thing about it. It isn't human, not matter how much it may look human, &amp; cannot truly grasp human morality using the ideals of the Courts as its guiding star, &amp; not factoring morality in its equations.<br /> Thankfully, it is not a fan of the plans of the Twilight Courts.<br /> Recently rumours have started to circulate that say that there are more of its kind, these ones bound to individual Court's, but again without a sense of human morality.<br /> <br /> Something designed by TFV &amp; chucked in a Black Box/Book(?) &quot;archive&quot;.<br /> It got picked out by someone, &amp; wormed into their brain taking over.<br /> It devours the Inner Light of Nobles, turning them back into unmagical humans for a time. The Inner Light will return thankfully.<br /> It's motives are unknown, but suspected to be a mixture of the Darkness' agenda &amp; TFV's agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T22:37:08-07:00","id":1379643,"title":"","content":"Wow. Another Princess-specific antagonist already. (I did not have this when I made the previous post.)<br /> <br /> A mass of Darkness that is described by some as a &quot;reverse-Noble&quot;. Created upon by the Blossoming of a regular Noble. Has this Noble's appearance, a warped version of their personality, &amp; a distorted, Darkness-focused version of their Calling. Maybe joins an anti-Court to contrast against whatever Court the Noble joins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":".  Grammer at first 04-09-2020, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:44:23-07:00","id":1379804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1375829#post1375829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Present a fully Developed Magister as a NPC Villain?</div> </div> </div> </div>As tempting as this is the last thing people need is any more encouragement to think of Darkness &amp; Light as a Princess antagonist book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:42:59-07:00","id":1379968,"title":"","content":"people have been doing that already?<br /> <br /> Another idea?<br /> <br /> Some kind of &quot;Redeeming&quot; Merit<br /> <br /> that shows your a bit more easily redeemed, or allows you to only suffer minor discomfort when exposed to Jade and Such<br /> <br /> oh Can the bless Charm that lets you enchant your fists with the power of Jade be used in the Dreamlands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 04-09-2020, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:38:42-07:00","id":1379989,"title":"","content":"As interesting as a &quot;redeeming&quot; merit is, I don't think that this is quite the right thread for it.<br /> For such a thing to be appropriate here, you would need to justify how it could turn up in a Night Horrors book.<br /> I've got nothing against the idea itself, I'm just pointing out that it doesn't fit here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T21:07:40-07:00","id":1380018,"title":"","content":"sorry Just Formori Freak legion h ad such Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts on some rules for Quantifying how much intel you can gain into the Darkness on earth by Defeating the Darkness in the Dreamlands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T16:23:22-07:00","id":1380514,"title":"","content":"Imagine if the Darkness had a leader, like there was some sort of hierarchy, &amp; that there was someone or something at the top.<br /> Meet the Mask of Darkness, it is that hypothetical top dog of the Darkness. It's not the top dog because it's stronger or smarter than all the rest, it's the top dog because it has a sense of overwhelming authority that makes every other creature &amp; person of the Darkness bend their knees to it.<br /> At least in theory. At the moment it's just a creepy-looking mask, until someone gets the bright idea to put it on.<br /> The mask doesn't take over people's bodies, it's not precisely the one running things here. What it does is play the Devil on your shoulder gig, slowly cutting away at your morality.<br /> The mask itself is also indestructible to nearly any form of harm, &amp; on the rare occasions when it gets broken it will just reform somewhere there's a sufficient quantity of the Darkness. When someone is wearing the mask it sort of melts into the person's body, removable only when the person wants it to come off, this gets rarer &amp; rarer over time.<br /> Praise the Lord there's only one of it. At least, we think there's only one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:39:06-07:00","id":1381741,"title":"","content":"When you go through a Tainted Areas Dark Door into the Dark Dream<br /> <br /> What happens if you Make a Successful Social lmaneuvering Roll on the figments you encounter?<br /> <br /> It seems like it should be a legitimate means to do so<br /> <br /> Let Graces and Troubadours shine.<br /> <br /> On one hand the figments are reflections of darkness<br /> <br /> on the other if you succeed in a roll You should be able to influence them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T08:33:42-07:00","id":1383372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1380514#post1380514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine if the Darkness had a leader, like there was some sort of hierarchy, &amp; that there was someone or something at the top.<br /> Meet the Mask of Darkness, it is that hypothetical top dog of the Darkness. It's not the top dog because it's stronger or smarter than all the rest, it's the top dog because it has a sense of overwhelming authority that makes every other creature &amp; person of the Darkness bend their knees to it.<br /> At least in theory. At the moment it's just a creepy-looking mask, until someone gets the bright idea to put it on.<br /> The mask doesn't take over people's bodies, it's not precisely the one running things here. What it does is play the Devil on your shoulder gig, slowly cutting away at your morality.<br /> The mask itself is also indestructible to nearly any form of harm, &amp; on the rare occasions when it gets broken it will just reform somewhere there's a sufficient quantity of the Darkness. When someone is wearing the mask it sort of melts into the person's body, removable only when the person wants it to come off, this gets rarer &amp; rarer over time.<br /> Praise the Lord there's only one of it. At least, we think there's only one...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T16:05:33-07:00","id":1384048,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on Social Maneuvering on Figments Created by Tainted places?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T15:50:59-07:00","id":1385146,"title":"","content":"A unique darkspawn that can home in on the Light even when the Nobles are in human mode. It doesn't know how it picks these targets or what connects them, it just knows that it has to kill them.<br /> Where does it come from? TFV? The Cheiron Group? Awakened experiments? Where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:53:01-07:00","id":1385178,"title":"","content":"I was reading the Princess the Hopeful Night Horror doc. earlier &amp; I came across the Unlights &amp; noticed significant similarities with the Court of Midnight which I came up with. I have come to the conclusion that you should not use both the Unlights &amp; the Court of Midnight at the same time in their current forms.<br /> A way for both of them to be used is to envision the Court of Midnight as an organized group of Unlights working together towards some nefarious goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T21:39:13-07:00","id":1385185,"title":"","content":"Fleshing out Saligia a bit here. This post is going to go over some powers unique to Saligia, as in the rest of the inhabitants of the Dark World can't utilize them.<br /> First, an explanation about the different powers. The various Mantles belong to the various Houses. Each House has their own Mantle, no one can wield a Mantle belonging to a House that they are not part of, &amp; no one can belong to multiple Houses.<br /> The Sorceries of the Peasants work very differently. Whereas the Mantles are powers that you assume &amp; utilize whenever, the Sorceries are visceral spells that must be cast, often this takes no time at all but still.<br /> <br /> The Mantles of the Ruling Houses<br /> The Mantle of Envy: the Mantle of Envy is about temporarily stealing Skills from other people. If the person you stole a Skill from dies, you automatically lose the Skill no matter how long it will be before the clock runs out.<br /> The Mantle of Gluttony: the Mantle of Gluttony allows you to consume any number of supernatural powers cast at you, adding up to your willpower, which you may &quot;vomit up&quot; later. There is a limit to how long you may keep a power if it is of the Light, wait too long &amp; it will start to burn you from the inside.<br /> The Mantle of Greed: with the Mantle of Greed you understand that everyone has a price &amp; grants you great skill in not only finding the prices of other people may be, but taking advantage of such knowledge.<br /> The Mantle of Lust: ...<br /> The Mantle of Pride: the Mantle of Pride is about not showing weaknesses or allowing such weaknesses to slow you down. Alternatively, it is about excelling in a chosen Skill beyond any normal limitations.<br /> The Mantle of Sloth: ...<br /> The Mantle of Wrath: the Mantle of Wrath is all about striking fast &amp; hard, doing as much damage as you can as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> I have done my best to come up with a power for each Mantle but sadly failed with the Mantle of Lust &amp; the Mantle of Sloth. You are welcome to fill in the gaps. Also, there should be multiple powers per Mantle, so feel free to come up with extras.<br /> <br /> Minor Houses include: Ambition; Apathy; Despair; Fraud; Shame; Treachery; Vanity; Violence<br /> Just because they're minor doesn't mean they don't have Mantles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 05-10-2020, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T21:43:31-07:00","id":1385187,"title":"","content":"Now some foes coming from Saligia. Just rehashing what Hunters are in this post, they are people from Saligia who temporarily leave their home country to hunt down Nobles so that Saligia may survive.<br /> <br /> A Hunter bearing the Mantle of Greed who succumbed to their greed when they saw the human world. They have abandoned Saligia &amp; plan to accumulate as much wealth &amp; possessions as possible.<br /> <br /> A lone Hunter who is the spawn of one of the seven ruling House Heads. They mean to make their House &amp; parent proud of them.<br /> <br /> A mini-province that is gearing up to make a play for power &amp; become one of the seven ruling House Heads, supplanting one of the current ones.<br /> <br /> A lone Hunter from peasant stock who plans to acquire a Noble &amp; use that Noble to elevate their peasant family.<br /> <br /> A legendarily successful team of Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":". 05-02-2020, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T21:57:41-07:00","id":1385189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1378848#post1378848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saligia: A small country located somewhere deep in the Dark World, far from any doors to the material world. Its presence here, so deep in the Dark World is a source of many rumours &amp; the rare Noble who conclusively knows (not someone who has just heard the rumours) of its existence is troubled by the knowledge.<br /> This country has a very visceral feel to it (maybe, not so sure about this point now).<br /> The people struggle day in &amp; day out just to survive here.<br /> It is an oligarchy, ruled by a council comprised of the heads of the seven most powerful families. These seven families are each governed by one of the seven deadly sins (envy, gluttony, greed, lust, pride, sloth, wrath).<br /> The country also has these &amp;quot;mini-provinces&amp;quot; embodying other negative concepts/ideas/etc. like apathy, despair, violence, vanity, fraud, treachery, etc. It is possible for one of the &amp;quot;mini-provinces&amp;quot; to get a set at the table of the big seven, thereby knocking down one of the current houses, it would be very hard however. Food for thought.<br /> A while ago, it was found that the Inner Light of a Noble could be used to help Saligia survive, &amp; the country sent out teams of warriors, trackers, beasts, etc. to find some &amp; bring them back.<br /> Once a Noble has been delivered back to Saliga, a bloody sacrifice is performed, harvesting the Inner Light for the good of Saligia.<br /> Unbeknownst to Saligia, whilst performing bloody sacrifices of the Nobles provides large, strong bursts, should a Noble set down to live in Saligia their Inner Light would constantly leak into the country, albeit at a slightly weaker level. Oh they may have heard the theory, but why take the risk when they've already got a strategy that works?</div> </div> </div> </div>More or less reposting the initial Saligia material. Explanation on what Hunters from Saligia are embedded within this mass of words, though now I see that I initially referred to them as &quot;warriors, trackers, beasts, etc.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T20:59:58-07:00","id":1385347,"title":"","content":"Think I can try to make the Circle of Clear Thought's Mystery Cult Merit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:33:40-07:00","id":1387222,"title":"","content":"Cheshires: semi-feline monsters, these darkspawn have a reputation for cruelty, sadism, &amp; a tendency to play with their prey. Their most famous powers are levitation, invisibility, &amp; limited teleportation. They can also draw power from deaths that they have a hand in causing. The only really good things about these monsters is that they are not particularly strong foes in physical combat &amp; they are universally solitary, despising their own kind.<br /> <br /> Gloriemic: a contagion that causes Nobles to start exemplifying the absolute extreme of whatever the ideology of their Court may be, without allowing for any other ideas. Curiously, it only affects Nobles pledged to Radiant Courts &amp; lowers the possibility to go Dethroned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:35:27-07:00","id":1387223,"title":"","content":"A Mnemosyne who has a YouTube channel. They have been using the channel to build a Cult of Darkness. An important step in bringing down the cult permanently would be shutting down the YouTube channel. <br /> \u25cf Channel/Account name: RememberingDarkness<br /> \u25cf Cult name: The Thousand Scattered Eyes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","user":"Krat05","date":".  Came up with a name for the cult 05-27-2020, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:22:50-07:00","id":1391604,"title":"","content":"I Really like the revised rules letting a darkened she pre acquired Umbrae and become a mneosmye<br /> <br /> It makes Mneosmye a bit less rare.<br /> <br /> The Darkness I think should largely be using hunters not fighting them<br /> <br /> I could see the sheer delight a Mighty Cataphract might feel on the last day in telling Hunters they helped to bring about the victory of the darkness by helping to remove the princesses.<br /> <br /> I think it would cripple the Stars of Bethlahem or Peoples guard with Grief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 05-25-2020, 11:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T21:05:17-07:00","id":1391856,"title":"","content":"Here's an incomplete writeup of a Princess character for this, and the Embassy she belongs to ... which, I warn you, you probably won't want to join.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Rp04neNAp3G6U9anL8UkkYrB0KPsTufNCAAl78-9nHw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Hespera, Ambassador to Blood</a><br /> <br /> There's two inspirations behind this. First, a remark in Requiem 2e on the Strix possessing supernaturals; and second, a character from a certain anime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-28T15:37:40-07:00","id":1392337,"title":"","content":"an idea I Had for a while?<br /> <br /> Counter investigation when a princess knows someones looking into her identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T04:17:36-07:00","id":1392780,"title":"","content":"Phew, finally back. Sorry to everyone, my computer broke and I had to wait for entire weeks for it to be fixed. Fear not, though, I have no intention to abandon this supplement.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to open my return, I started working a bit more and fleshing out the Howler/Mazkin entrance, using the sketch as a basis. Might need some help to work on the mechanics, though. Both for them and others.<br /> <br /> Now for the ideas suggested:<br /> <br /> Cheshires: I like the idea.Probably something to work on.<br /> <br /> Glomeric: ... Interesting idea, though might need to be fleshed out a bit.<br /> <br /> Hespera: Absolutely <i>love</i> it. With Micheal Brazier's permission, I'd like to add her to the supplement.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T17:44:35-07:00","id":1393265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1375152-princess-the-hopeful-night-horror-supplement?p=1392780#post1392780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hespera: Absolutely <i>love</i> it. With Micheal Brazier's permission, I'd like to add her to the supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means! That's why I worked her up.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what her Attributes, Skills and Merits should be - feel free to flesh those out. I think she's Mental/Social/Physical. Lemure I see as a Gangrel who supplies brawn when that's required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T06:53:31-07:00","id":1393409,"title":"","content":"Ok I have to ask a noob question......wtf if Princess? Admitting I have no clue what this is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:06:59-07:00","id":1393529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon 